{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game","id":43270,"title":"Running my first game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-05T18:51:41-08:00","id":43270,"title":"Running my first game","content":"I've been playing nWoD for about 2 years now, and have been tossing around the idea of running my own game. I finally got some more inquiries from our party this weekend, so I've decided to really start working on putting something together.<br /> So far I've decided that everyone will be Changelings, and that the setting is going to be somewhere in the either Washington or Oregon. I want to run a mystery campaign with lots of disappearances.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any insight or suggestions for a first time Storyteller, it would be much appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T21:57:39-08:00","id":43351,"title":"","content":"I think I'm going to make each session have a fairy tale element to it. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T03:04:23-08:00","id":43413,"title":"","content":"I was going to write some notes earlier, but I got kind of distracted.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, know what you're comfortable with - I learned STing Changeling while playing with players who both knew the system better than I did, but also had more experience running games.<br /> <br /> Don't be afraid to veto things! Changeling has a lot of material (although it pales in comparison to Vampire) which you might not be comfortable with or knowledgeable at how it works yet. The level of knowledge you need to run a game is a lot more than if you're just playing. You're allowed to go 'Nothing but the core book's contracts/merits/kiths' or something.<br /> <br /> Allow yourself to experiment - I tried a lot of things until I got comfortable in my slot, some worked and I kept them, others didn't and I didn't.<br /> <br /> Make sure you clearly manage player expectations of your players...I was fairly frank about the fact I was new and wanted to learn, so I think my players had a bit more fun with it than if they were expecting an experienced ST with no other context. Likewise, I kept asking them for feedback and help and I usually got it. Even from a 'I'm not/am enjoying playing this character' perspective.<br /> <br /> Take notes! (Unless your memory is perfect, then you don't need to). They're useful when you need to remember something eight sessions down the line.<br /> <br /> Also, you've picked a great game to start <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Changeling is excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:03:05-08:00","id":43524,"title":"","content":"Dreams are important in Changeling. Give them dreams. In my changeling game, I had four PCs. Each session, one PC got a prophetic dream, one got a weird dream, one got a dream about their durance, and one got a dream about their fetch. Of course, they could never quite tell which was which...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:46:03-08:00","id":43876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=43413#post43413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to write some notes earlier, but I got kind of distracted.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, know what you're comfortable with - I learned STing Changeling while playing with players who both knew the system better than I did, but also had more experience running games.<br /> <br /> Don't be afraid to veto things! Changeling has a lot of material (although it pales in comparison to Vampire) which you might not be comfortable with or knowledgeable at how it works yet. The level of knowledge you need to run a game is a lot more than if you're just playing. You're allowed to go 'Nothing but the core book's contracts/merits/kiths' or something.<br /> <br /> Allow yourself to experiment - I tried a lot of things until I got comfortable in my slot, some worked and I kept them, others didn't and I didn't.<br /> <br /> Make sure you clearly manage player expectations of your players...I was fairly frank about the fact I was new and wanted to learn, so I think my players had a bit more fun with it than if they were expecting an experienced ST with no other context. Likewise, I kept asking them for feedback and help and I usually got it. Even from a 'I'm not/am enjoying playing this character' perspective.<br /> <br /> Take notes! (Unless your memory is perfect, then you don't need to). They're useful when you need to remember something eight sessions down the line.<br /> <br /> Also, you've picked a great game to start <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Changeling is excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're actually doing a full vampire game right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In our party, I know more about Changelings than anyone, and am still reading up on more stuff. Since this will be the first time anyone other than me has played a Changeling, we're going to take it slow and all kind of learn together. But everyone seems excited about it and my boyfriend is our current ST and he has promised to help me with anything I need.<br /> I have a whole document in my writing program set up with all sorts of notes already. Each NPC has their own file, I've got files for enemies, I'm going to have a file on each PC, all sorts of stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thank you for all the insight! I really appreciate it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:47:49-08:00","id":43878,"title":"","content":"The dreams thing gave me a very good idea. I know I'm going to have to work dreams into th game somehow, but wasn't sure what to do with them. That helped me a lot. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T18:28:20-08:00","id":49423,"title":"","content":"I've been running Changeling ongoing campaigns for a couple of years now. I love using fairy tale and mythic themes, characters, and tokens. One way I've used fairy tales is to help inspire me to imagine what Durance was like for each character. As part of character creation, I ask them to pick out their character's favorite fairy tale when s/he was a child. In my version of Changeling, fairy tales are Keeper propaganda, so instead of being the protagonist, I imagine the human-turned-fey as a side character or villain of the story. For example, if a player picked Beauty and the Beast, I would likely make them an Elemental Manikin-- so s/he would play a role in the Keeper's household like <i>Lumi\u00e8re or </i>r Mrs. Potts, rather than Belle. Someone chose Peter Pan, so his Keeper was the most terrifying tyrant than regressed people and assigned them roles (lost boy, pirate, Indian) and made them battle each other for his amusement (this is not too far off from the original).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T23:13:10-08:00","id":49582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=49423#post49423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been running Changeling ongoing campaigns for a couple of years now. I love using fairy tale and mythic themes, characters, and tokens. One way I've used fairy tales is to help inspire me to imagine what Durance was like for each character. As part of character creation, I ask them to pick out their character's favorite fairy tale when s/he was a child. In my version of Changeling, fairy tales are Keeper propaganda, so instead of being the protagonist, I imagine the human-turned-fey as a side character or villain of the story. For example, if a player picked Beauty and the Beast, I would likely make them an Elemental Manikin-- so s/he would play a role in the Keeper's household like <i>Lumi\u00e8re or </i>r Mrs. Potts, rather than Belle. Someone chose Peter Pan, so his Keeper was the most terrifying tyrant than regressed people and assigned them roles (lost boy, pirate, Indian) and made them battle each other for his amusement (this is not too far off from the original).</div> </div> </div> </div>I may just have to do something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:45:43-08:00","id":50178,"title":"","content":"As a primary ST for my group with Changeling being one of my favorites (was finally trumped by Demon) I can let you know of a few pitfalls that I had to work through.<br /> <br /> Players:<ul><li>\u200bAs previously stated, don't be afraid to veto. A player may want something that you are neither prepared for or it would massively complicate the story or run diagonally to what you have created. It's OK to outright say <b>no, </b>after all, you know more about what is coming up then they do and they may not know that the thing they want will make the entire game unbearable to them. Also things like: wanting some cross-over stuff (regular access to the Underworld but you are playing changeling) is all up to you to decide whether your setting can handle it (and whether it would ruin the themes).</li> <li>near contrary to the former, don't be afraid to change your story for the players. If you are using Aspirations these are invaluable for that purpose. If you notice they move in a different direction then your plot (or seem to have fun with something else that wasn't really included in your plot) than don't be afraid to change your plot to fit their level of fun or, if the case may be, completely change the plot. Remember the game is about having fun (it's simple but during game, you have no idea how easy it is to simply deny players and railroad their characters. it's hard to keep up with them rather than to make them fit the story)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:18:37-08:00","id":50819,"title":"","content":"I love to talk about characters and plot, but I was thinking about what I would have liked to know before starting my first Changeling campaign.... The main text is desperately hard to navigate and the index is terrible. I've added post-it page markers to make access faster, which helps a lot when players new to the system have questions. The contracts in the main book are of limited use and frustrated my players who were used to less subtle magic-- the antidote to this is the Winter Masques supplement. The seeming contracts are much, much more practical and fun for players. Also, the expanded kiths are fun and fill in some obvious gaps in the original (e.g. you couldn't be a traditional &quot;tinkerbell&quot; type of fairy in the original). Even better for the Storyteller though, Winter Masques talks about about Durance in a way that gives you clear ideas about what could have happened to the characters and how it would be different for each seeming (which in turn means that offering them glimpses of their past through dreams gets a lot easier). <br /> <br /> The Autumn Nights supplement is all antagonists, which is good for the ST, but I was frustrated that it was not very easy to just grab a villain and run him/her on the go. There aren't that many antagonists per chapter and for my purposes, I needed to make some changes with them before I used them (also the layout for these NPCs is not great and it's hard to just glance at the book and use the stats for battle). I just didn't find it well written and only moderately helpful as a ST (when it looked like it would be very helpful).<br /> <br /> What did help me a lot was getting the Fearmaker's Promise Module and running that very early in the campaign. Throughout my role playing, I've rarely used or played in modules, but Fearmaker helped me by summing up several of the members of a Changeling court and offered up several antagonists that were shades of grey-- and one scary minor Keeper with an interesting, loose plot. I filled out the material with more Hedge encounters and more court members and it became part of the campaign foundation. The module helped me think in a different way about how to prep for a game, what kind of info is really needed for NPCs and how to get players to reflect on their choices in the game.<br /> <br /> If you get Rites of Spring, it will explain more fully many elements mentioned in the original book-- for example, what is the magic of the mask? Does it work on all of the senses? Does the mask change with your Wyrd? Also, there is an alternative set of rules for vows and oaths that makes them a lot simpler and easier to incorporate as a regular part of changeling life. The Hollow merits offered in this book are great and if your players find out about them, they will beg you to use the supplement (build Baba Yaga's hut? Yes, you can!). It is by far the least organized book with useless chapter titles and no index. You need to read it cover to cover and make your own page number notes-- I'm a academic and I find that tedious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T23:10:27-08:00","id":52172,"title":"","content":"I have all of the changeling books, and have glanced through most of them. Post-it notes are very much my friends. Lol. My boyfriend suggested I might run Fear Maker's Promise just to get a feel of things, so I might wind up switching things up and doing that. I opened Winter Masques to all my players, but did veto a few kiths, and I've pulled most of my NPCs from that book. I have high hopes for the game, and I really do appreciate everyone's input. Though if all else fails, a friend of mine gave me some pretty invaluable advice, especially since very few of the players are clear on the rules. He told me that if I get stuck to &quot;Just roll some dice and make stuff up.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:37:48-08:00","id":52224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roanscribbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=52172#post52172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if all else fails, a friend of mine gave me some pretty invaluable advice, especially since very few of the players are clear on the rules. He told me that if I get stuck to &quot;Just roll some dice and make stuff up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be completely honest - that actually works better than it should most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T06:51:48-08:00","id":52340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roanscribbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=52172#post52172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have all of the changeling books, and have glanced through most of them. Post-it notes are very much my friends. Lol. My boyfriend suggested I might run Fear Maker's Promise just to get a feel of things, so I might wind up switching things up and doing that. I opened Winter Masques to all my players, but did veto a few kiths, and I've pulled most of my NPCs from that book. I have high hopes for the game, and I really do appreciate everyone's input. Though if all else fails, a friend of mine gave me some pretty invaluable advice, especially since very few of the players are clear on the rules. He told me that if I get stuck to &quot;Just roll some dice and make stuff up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the advice part, but personally I would not bother with te rolling dice step. If I was going to just make stuff up, then the dice aren't reall telling me anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:16:13-08:00","id":52473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GitariArt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=52340#post52340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the advice part, but personally I would not bother with te rolling dice step. If I was going to just make stuff up, then the dice aren't reall telling me anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if I have an antagonist who is about to open combat, or is going to manipulate the party in some way, making sure they legitimately succeed on their rolls would keep my party from calling me on bs. Or, just rolling dice and not letting them know what it was for is a decent way to screw with them when I need to buy some time. Our current ST has used this trick a lot, especially in social settings when someone is trying to find out if an NPC is lying. The NPC would be telling the truth, someone would roll to see if they were lying, our ST would roll, then say, &quot;Yeah, you think he's telling the truth.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T14:54:41-08:00","id":52780,"title":"","content":"That advice is wonderful for almost any game, but I find it especially fits Changeling. The game revolves around characters who have good reason for paranoia about the nature of the world around them, and the impact on it by vastly potent beings for inscrutable, arbitrary reasons. An ST making a lot of rolls that may or may not govern anything and then not explaining them feels perfectly in theme. Also adds a bit of an edge to a horror game. Nothing Is Scarier, and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T23:46:17-08:00","id":53753,"title":"","content":"I decided tonight to ban guns and other such explosives from my game. Several people in our group are 'run in and kill it as fast as we can' types, so I thought it would be better to ban guns outright in order to make them focus more on their powers. I'm am going to have each court leader have a contract in place counteracting the explosives, but only within the city. Their reasoning behind this is so that if humans ever tried to come in and wipe out the changeling population, they would have a harder time without guns.<br /> Now I just need to come up with a few repercussions the town will face as the game is set in modern times, and guns and such work just fine outside the barrier specified by the contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:31:22-08:00","id":53845,"title":"","content":"I don't know how effective that would be. One of the characters in my group is a policeman, prefers to focus on his magic for combat when facing fae opponents though. He has some points in Firearms and due to the city's anti-biker gang laws he's even allowed to keep an Assault Rifle for self-defence. However, nothing he can do can match the damage output of the dual-wielding master swordsman in the group. The swordsman hardly uses any powers, just one of the Contracts of Hearth to get a +4 on his first attack roll. Other than that, the most supernatural thing about him is that he used pledges to get his Weaponry skill up to 5 early on.<br /> <br /> If they're close enough to engage in melee, and the opponent's defence/armour aren't too over the top, then there's probably not going to be much difference between a Changeling using a rifle and a Changeling dual-wielding melee weapons. Or, indeed, a human in either case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:38:09-08:00","id":54020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=53845#post53845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how effective that would be.<br /> <br /> If they're close enough to engage in melee, and the opponent's defence/armour aren't too over the top, then there's probably not going to be much difference between a Changeling using a rifle and a Changeling dual-wielding melee weapons. Or, indeed, a human in either case.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense... I've just noticed that in our current game (all vampires) that any time someone tries to hold a conversation with a potential antagonist for more than two turns, half our party goes, &quot;Well I'm sick of waiting while they try to talk it out, I'm going to shoot the bad guy.&quot; or they don't even bother trying to talk they immediately rush in with guns blazing, or they walk up and punch the NPC. Even if they're supposed to be the social character. We almost had someone rage-quit last night because of that exact thing.<br /> It's just really frustrating, and I'm trying to find a way around it. I don't want all of the games to be pretty much the same thing over and over again. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T09:44:16-08:00","id":54060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roanscribbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=54020#post54020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That makes sense... I've just noticed that in our current game (all vampires) that any time someone tries to hold a conversation with a potential antagonist for more than two turns, half our party goes, &quot;Well I'm sick of waiting while they try to talk it out, I'm going to shoot the bad guy.&quot; or they don't even bother trying to talk they immediately rush in with guns blazing, or they walk up and punch the NPC. Even if they're supposed to be the social character. We almost had someone rage-quit last night because of that exact thing. It's just really frustrating, and I'm trying to find a way around it. I don't want all of the games to be pretty much the same thing over and over again. :/</div> </div> </div> </div> It seems like there isn't an honest dialogue between the GM and the players over what kind of game everyone wants to play. I think it is important, that before the game actually begins, everyone sits down together to talk about what sorta expectations people have concerning the game. It is not the players fault for wanting to play an action game. Nor is it wrong for the GM to focus on dialogue and plot. Discussion concerning this social contract is imperative for everyone having fun, and it is the role of the GM to ensure that no one is excluded. If a combat loving player is assured at least 4 awesome combat scenarios per story, he maybe more willing to let social encounters unfold naturally ... After all, he knows that he will have his time to shine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T09:56:25-08:00","id":54063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=54060#post54060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It seems like there isn't an honest dialogue between the GM and the players over what kind of game everyone wants to play. I think it is important, that before the game actually begins, everyone sits down together to talk about what sorta expectations people have concerning the game. It is not the players fault for wanting to play an action game. Nor is it wrong for the GM to focus on dialogue and plot. Discussion concerning this social contract is imperative for everyone having fun, and it is the role of the GM to ensure that no one is excluded. If a combat loving player is assured at least 4 awesome combat scenarios per story, he maybe more willing to let social encounters unfold naturally ... After all, he knows that he will have his time to shine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our current GM is pretty flexible, it's just that some party members built their characters around a more social focus, and some members were actually banned from making a complete combat monkey in this game and were told they had to build social characters, but they found ways around it and now our entire group is once again all combat based (except for my character who is just sneaky and quiet) but when I run my changeling game I want to have something other than non-stop combat. I've built in multiple combat scenes into all of my plots so far, but I'm just trying to cut back on their ability to rush in and kill everything, because that will wind up biting them later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T09:58:55-08:00","id":54065,"title":"","content":"That's... a tricky problem to work around. In that it might be more a problem of &quot;different parts of the group just want different or even mutually exclusive things.&quot; Some players are really into taking that approach in a game, don't see the appeal in any others, and aren't <i>going</i> to see that appeal even if you make them do it. There's nothing wrong with anyone's wants, everyone just has a different idea of what's fun and what's not, and those of multiple people aren't always going to overlap. It's just something that may produce conflict and it may not even be obvious as an issue to all involved. Doesn't necessarily mean that's the situation you've got, but I do recommend having a discussion on the topic. While you've likely tried it already, talking things out like that, trying to find a compromise or some other way to deal with it on the player-level will likely work better than any character-/game-level solution.<br /> <br /> That said, further talk on the atmosphere may not hurt. Changeling has a lot of deals and bargains spun around, so most characters have a lot of connections and ties to other people, organizations, and the like. As a result, killing any given person -- or even making the attempt or harming them -- is very likely to get a number of those affected parties on the heroes' cases. Maybe try to convey to your trigger-happy players that the threat any given NPC represents may be WAY bigger than their personal combat prowess, and that this threat may not merely extend beyond their death/defeat but may be fully realized through it. Doesn't mean violence or lethal force are never useful tools, they just need some careful consideration.<br /> <br /> Again, I think it's likely a social issue that needs talking out if it's to be solved. If they find social dealings way too boring to go on, just pointing out that non-immediate danger may not make it any less boring for them. It may just frustrate them into feeling their hands are tied and the campaign's railroaded.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And boy was I slow on the draw, there. ^_^o Seconding everything Firefly Night had to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:23:19-08:00","id":54072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=54065#post54065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, further talk on the atmosphere may not hurt. Changeling has a lot of deals and bargains spun around, so most characters have a lot of connections and ties to other people, organizations, and the like. As a result, killing any given person -- or even making the attempt or harming them -- is very likely to get a number of those affected parties on the heroes' cases. Maybe try to convey to your trigger-happy players that the threat any given NPC represents may be WAY bigger than their personal combat prowess, and that this threat may not merely extend beyond their death/defeat but may be fully realized through it. Doesn't mean violence or lethal force are never useful tools, they just need some careful consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you guys for the suggestions. I will definitely explain to them that NPCs' influences stretch far and wide in this game, and that is something they will need to take into consideration. Especially when I put them up against changelings who have high ranks in various courts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T14:55:15-08:00","id":54240,"title":"","content":"I have run into similar scenarios in my games (the aforementioned master swordsman regards most obstacles as something to be removed with his swords). The other members of the group take a much more balanced approach to the game, which is good. As a result of him starting fights in inappropriate situations, friendly NPCs regard the swordsman as reckless at best, and an unbalanced idiot bringing far too much mortal attention to the Freehold at worst. I'm reasonably bullheaded when it comes to how events play out as well. If the characters kill the only person who could have told them how to stop the evil man's plan, then the evil man's plan will probably go ahead and the players will have to cope with the fallout. Actions should have consequences. It is treading a fine line between that and railroading, I suppose, but I tend to believe that if the players willfully sabotage the chances of their own success just to feel like a badass then they should have to copy with the ramifications.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that I have asked the players not to aim for ludicrously high levels in combat skills in the past, but I quickly found that it just doesn't work in Changeling. Three quick pledges can take an average fighter to the edge of mastery. Playing up the social ramifications of violence, as suggested, has been considerably more successful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:12:39-08:00","id":54295,"title":"","content":"I come from a theatre background, and I have found that the rules of improv are invaluable to anyone wanting to run an engaging game.<br /> <br /> The following are the rules:<br /> 1) Say Yes-and!<br /> For a story to be built, whether it is short form or long form, the players have to agree to the basic situation and set-up. The who, what, and where have to be developed for a scene to work.<br /> <br /> 2) After the `and` add new information.<br /> An improvised scene can't move forward or advance unless we add new information. That is why new information is added after the Yes of Yes-and!<br /> <br /> 3) Don't Block.<br /> The opposite of saying yes-and is blocking or denial. A good GM will not shut down players and take away their agency.<br /> <br /> 4) Avoid Questions.<br /> A form of blocking (in its more subtle form) is asking questions. Questions force our partners to fill in the information or do the work. It is a way of avoiding committing to a choice or a detail. It is playing it safe. However, on more advanced levels, questions can be used to add information or tell your players the direction to go in.<br /> <br /> 5) Focus on the Here and Now.<br /> Another useful rule is to keep the focus on the here and now. A scene is about the people in the scene. The change, the struggle, the win or loss will happen to the characters in the scene. Focus on what is going on right this at this moment.<br /> <br /> 6) Establish the Location!<br /> Good scenes take place somewhere and at sometime. They do not take place on an empty stage. A location can easily be established in one or two lines without breaking the scene.<br /> <br /> 7) Be Specific- Provide Details!<br /> Details are the lifeblood of moving a scene forward. Each detail provides clues to what is important. Details help provide beat objectives and flesh out characters.<br /> <br /> 8) Change, Change, Change!<br /> Improv is about character change. The characters in a scene must experience some type of change for the scene to be interesting. Characters need to go on journeys, be altered by revelations, experience the ramifications of their choices and be moved by emotional moments.<br /> <br /> 9) For serious and emotional scenes, focus on characters and relationships.<br /> A long form improv set should contain a variety of scenes. Some scenes will be emotional, some will be tense, and some should be funny. The easiest way to make a scene serious is by focusing on the relationship of those on the stage (their characters).<br /> <br /> 10) For humor, commit and take choices to the nth degree or focus on actions/objects.<br /> A good long form set is balanced. Shakespeare knew that too much pathos was wearing on the audience; hence, he had minor characters in humorous scenes such as the drunken porter in MacBeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 01-20-2014, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:32:06-08:00","id":54680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=54060#post54060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It seems like there isn't an honest dialogue between the GM and the players over what kind of game everyone wants to play. I think it is important, that before the game actually begins, everyone sits down together to talk about what sorta expectations people have concerning the game. It is not the players fault for wanting to play an action game. Nor is it wrong for the GM to focus on dialogue and plot. Discussion concerning this social contract is imperative for everyone having fun, and it is the role of the GM to ensure that no one is excluded. If a combat loving player is assured at least 4 awesome combat scenarios per story, he maybe more willing to let social encounters unfold naturally ... After all, he knows that he will have his time to shine.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wise old GM once said, &quot;do not try to solve out-of-game attitudes with in-game changes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night\">Firefly Night</a> is dead on, discuss the social aspects of the game everyone enjoys and move forward with out of game changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":2062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","user":"Arref","date":". 01-21-2014, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:09:34-08:00","id":55559,"title":"","content":"Grimm, the tv show, will give you a ton of ideas for incorporating the fairies into the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2073-mctroll","name":"McTroll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2073_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:55:53-08:00","id":55591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McTroll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/43270-running-my-first-game?p=55559#post55559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grimm, the tv show, will give you a ton of ideas for incorporating the fairies into the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have TV...and what little bit I have seen of that show terrified me. But thank you for the suggestion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:29:59-08:00","id":55791,"title":"","content":"Grimm is on Hulu and the recent season is the best so far. Not thta that helps if it's tooscary for you. Once Upon A Time is also on Hulu and has some usable story elements. Lost Girl is Netflix instant view, but is probably as scary as Grimm.<br /> <br /> On a much raider interpretation, I like to watch The Mentalist (on disc from Netflix) and imagine the lead actor as a Bright One or some other Fairest. In fact I find it useful to reinterpret every movie/story/etc as if I was just seeing the Masks of changeling main characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}